# Ctrl+Break in the shell in C (roadmap os-server.md P9): cat, reading the
# terminal, gets SIGINT, whose default action ends it; the shell, init's
# child, goes on, and $? says 128 + 2. The keys after Ctrl+Break wait for
# cat's end: typed at once, they could reach cat's read, still pending.
program: sh
# DOSBox-X has no disk controller rx286 can use (docs/emulators.md).
emulators: bochs mame
keys: cat\n{wait 20}{ctrl-break}{wait 20}echo $?\n
---
rx286, test build
/a$ cat
rx286: Ctrl+Break: SIGINT
/a$ echo $?
130
/a$
